  "proposedEffectivePlan" : "Play D3 and win the opening lead in South. There are eight immediate winners: two diamonds, two hearts, one spade and three clubs. Develop a fourth club for nine; a 3–2 club break supplies a fifth club as well. Cash CA and CK, following with dummy’s small clubs, then lead a low club to CQ. Against any 3–2 or 4–1 break this establishes at least four club tricks after at most one concession. If necessary, return from dummy with a low heart to HA and surrender a club, retaining the remaining diamond honor and SA as controls. Recover the lead and cash the established clubs, HK and the remaining side-suit winners. Do not spend those controls unnecessarily before clubs are established. If the first club round reveals a 5–0 break, reassess the club sequence using the known location and spot cards before cashing the second honor; nine tricks may then require an additional source. Prioritize securing nine over speculative overtricks."
